  "title": "Erdős Problem #992",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $x_1<x_2<\\cdots$ be an infinite sequence of integers. Is it true that, for almost all $\\alpha \\in [0,1]$, the discrepancy $ D(N)=\\max_{I\\subseteq [0,1]} \\lvert \\#\\{ n\\leq N : \\{ \\alpha x_n\\}\\in I\\} - \\lvert I\\rvert N\\rvert $ satisfies $ D(N) \\ll N^{1/2}(\\log N)^{o(1)}? $ Or even $ D(N)\\ll N^{1/2}(\\log\\log N)^{O(1)}? $ ",
    "sha256": "530ee3dfc82110edd1b7ede39b4a7984826c6a88953afc4aa3d44d1929b4bd02",
